[al:新概念英语第三册]
[ti:45. The Power of the Press]
[00:00.440] Passage 45. | 课文45。
[00:02.035] The power of the press. | 报刊的力量。
[00:04.420] In democratic countries, | 在民主国家，
[00:06.570] any efforts to restrict the freedom of the press are rightly condemned. | 任何限制新闻自由的努力都理所当然地受到谴责。
[00:10.415] However, this freedom can easily be abused. | 然而，这种自由很容易被滥用。
[00:13.500] Stories about people | 关于人们的故事
[00:15.310] often attract far more public attention than political events. | 常常比政治事件更能吸引公众的注意力。
[00:19.140] Though we may enjoy reading about the lives of others, | 尽管我们可能喜欢阅读别人的生活，
[00:22.245] it is extremely doubtful whether we would equally enjoy reading about ourselves. | 但我们是否会同样喜欢阅读我们自己的生活，这是非常值得怀疑的。
[00:26.042] but from baby food and soap manufacturers who wished to advertise their products. | 还来自那些希望宣传自己产品的婴儿食品和肥皂制造商。
[00:27.700] Acting on the contention that facts are sacred, | 秉持事实神圣不可侵犯的论点，
[00:30.280] reporters can cause untold suffering to individuals | 记者们通过公布个人私生活的细节，
[00:33.730] by publishing details about their private lives. | 可能会给他们造成无法言喻的痛苦。
[00:36.645] Newspapers exert such tremendous influence | 报纸施加着如此巨大的影响，
[00:39.665] that they can not only bring about major changes to the lives of ordinary people, | 以至于它们不仅能给普通人的生活带来重大改变，
[00:43.645] but can even overthrow a government. | 甚至可以推翻一个政府。
[00:46.345] The story of a poor family that acquired fame and fortune overnight | 一个贫困家庭一夜之间获得名望和财富的故事，
[00:50.895] dramatically illustrates the power of the press. | 生动地说明了报刊的力量。
[00:53.970] The family lived in Aberdeen, | 这个家庭住在阿伯丁，
[00:56.280] a small town of 23,000 inhabitants in South Dakota. | 一个位于南达科他州，拥有2.3万居民的小镇。
[01:00.535] As the parents had five children, | 由于这对父母有五个孩子，
[01:03.025] life was a perpetual struggle against poverty. | 生活是一场与贫困的无休止的斗争。
[01:06.040] They were expecting their sixth child, | 他们正期待着第六个孩子，
[01:08.675] and were faced with even more pressing economic problems. | 并面临着更加紧迫的经济问题。
[01:12.170] If they had had only one more child, | 如果他们只多了一个孩子，
[01:14.680] the fact would have passed unnoticed. | 这件事就会被忽视。
[01:16.815] They would have continued to struggle against economic odds, | 他们将继续与经济困境作斗争，
[01:19.905] and would have lived in obscurity. | 并默默无闻地生活。
[01:22.015] But they suddenly became the parents of quintuplets, | 但是他们突然成了五胞胎的父母，
[01:25.360] four girls and a boy, | 四个女孩和一个男孩，
[01:26.97] an event which radically changed their lives. | 这一事件彻底改变了他们的生活。
[01:30.080] The day after the birth of the five children, | 五个孩子出生后的第二天，
[01:32.975] an aeroplane arrived in Aberdeen, | 一架飞机抵达阿伯丁，
[01:34.899] bringing 60 reporters and photographers. | 载来了60名记者和摄影师。
[01:37.58] The news was of national importance, | 这个消息具有全国性的重要意义，
[01:40.005] for the poor couple had become the parents of the only quintuplets in America. | 因为这对贫困夫妇成了美国唯一的五胞胎的父母。
[01:45.315] The rise to fame was swift. | 成名之路迅速展开。
[01:48.550] Television cameras and newspapers | 电视摄像机和报纸
[01:50.650] carried the news to everyone in the country. | 将这一消息传遍了全国各地。
[01:53.190] Newspapers and magazines | 报纸和杂志
[01:55.135] offered the family huge sums | 向这个家庭提供了巨额资金，
[01:57.06] for the exclusive rights to publish stories and photographs. | 以获取独家发表新闻和照片的权利。
[02:00.600] Gifts poured in, | 礼物如潮水般涌来，
[02:02.340] not only from unknown people, | 不仅来自不认识的人，
[02:04.305] but from baby food and soap manufacturers who wished to advertise their products. | 还来自那些希望宣传自己产品的婴儿食品和肥皂制造商。
[02:08.980] The old farmhouse the family lived in | 这个家庭居住的旧农舍
[02:11.435] was to be replaced by a new $100,000 home. | 将被一栋价值10万美元的新房取代。
[02:14.965] Reporters kept pressing for interviews, | 记者们不停地要求采访，
[02:17.61] so lawyers had to be employed to act as spokesmen for the family at press conferences. | 因此不得不雇佣律师在新闻发布会上担任这个家庭的发言人。
[02:22.545] The event brought serious changes to the town itself. | 这一事件给小镇本身带来了巨大的变化。
[02:26.060] Plans were announced to build a huge new highway, | 宣布了修建一条大型新高速公路的计划，
[02:29.505] as Aberdeen was now likely to attract thousands of tourists. | 因为阿伯丁现在很可能会吸引成千上万的游客。
[02:33.37] Signposts erected on the outskirts of the town | 竖立在小镇郊区的路标
[02:36.450] directed tourists not to Aberdeen, | 指引游客不是去阿伯丁，
[02:38.70] but to Quint City, USA. | 而是去美国五胞胎城。
[02:41.760] The local authorities discussed the possibility of erecting a Quint Museum | 当地政府讨论了建立一个五胞胎博物馆的可能性，
[02:46.72] to satisfy the curiosity of the public | 以满足公众的好奇心，
[02:49.160] and to protect the family from inquisitive tourists. | 并保护这个家庭免受好奇游客的打扰。
[02:52.450] While the five babies were still quietly sleeping in oxygen tents in a hospital nursery, | 当五个婴儿还在医院育儿室的氧气帐篷里安静地睡觉时，
[02:58.055] their parents were paying the price for fame. | 他们的父母正在为名声付出代价。
[03:01.240] It would never again be possible for them to lead normal lives. | 他们将再也无法过上正常的生活。
[03:05.510] They had become the victims of commercialization, | 他们成了商业化的受害者，
[03:08.755] for their names had acquired a market value. | 因为他们的名字已经获得了市场价值。
[03:11.740] The town itself received so much attention | 这个小镇本身受到了如此多的关注，
[03:15.20] that almost every one of the inhabitants was affected to a greater or less degree. | 以至于几乎每个居民都受到了一定程度的影响。